From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 09:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 60/60] PC5: the crash report names a C++ exception and shows the
 code at the fault (Wine patch 0939)

A game's engine that stopped itself with a C++ exception it didn't catch
was reported only by the exception's code and address (Call of Juarez
Gunslinger, the same in every log). Wine's crash report now names the
exception's type and, for a std::exception, its message. A fault on an
instruction the console refuses showed only as a read of FFFFFFFF (Far
Cry's CrySystem.dll): the report now has the flags register and the
code at the fault, so the next log says which instruction it was. Both
only add lines to a report that is made anyway.
